# Customers

## Summary

The customers a project keeps (the backend calls them entities): private people, companies, public bodies, and the organisations themselves, of the types the project configures. A customer has a type, a salutation, a gender, a title, a first and a last name, a company or organisation name, a tax number, an e-mail address, phone numbers, the languages they speak, the customer groups they are in, addresses, the attribute values the project configures for their type, wallets and files. A customer belongs to the organisation of the staff member who created it. Staff with the customers role list the customers, filter them, create them, keep customer groups, change a customer's details, addresses, attributes, wallets and files, read the e-mails and push notifications sent to them, and delete them. An organisation also has its payment account with its fees, and its API keys.

The parts only some projects use are switched by the project: the tabs an opened customer shows by the options it gives the library, and the calling-number fields, the "Customer group" column and other modules' buttons by the backend's `amgshop` configuration.

## Requirements

- **ENTROLE** — The module needs `entities:role`. Creating a customer needs its `create` permission; changing a customer, its addresses, its attribute values and its files needs `update`; deleting a customer or a file needs `delete`; opening a file needs `read`. The backend refuses each operation without its permission — from [juicebar#Requirements[ROLES]]
- **ENTORG** — A customer belongs to the organisation the staff member who created it was signed in to. The listing shows staff the customers of the organisation they are signed in to; a customer is opened, changed or deleted only when it belongs to that organisation or is that organisation's own record. A super admin of customers (`entities:role#super-admin`) lists, opens, changes and deletes the customers of every organisation. Where the backend configuration of `entities` sets `strictTenancy` off, opening, changing and deleting are not checked this way.
- **ENTPROTECT** — A customer created as "Customer only visible for me" is protected by the staff member who created it. Where the backend configuration of `entities` sets `protection` on, the listing shows a protected customer only to that staff member, to admins of customers (`entities:role#admin`) and to super admins; without `protection` everyone with the role sees it.
- **ENTTYPES** — The `entities:juicebox:settings` configuration gives the customer types: each a name, a value and the columns the listing shows for it. The names are shown in the admin's language where the module's dictionary has them. The customers of type `organisation` are listed only for admins and super admins of customers.
- **ENTNAME** — The module names a customer by first name and last name; a customer without both by its company or organisation name; a customer with neither has no name.
- **ENTCOUNTRY** — The countries to choose from are the admin's own list, named in the admin's language. A customer's country is the country of its first address.
- **ENTAMG** — Where the backend has an `amgshop` configuration, the create and the details form have a calling-number field before the phone and before the mobile phone, kept with the customer's attributes, and the listing has a "Customer group" column and shows the page buttons the project's other modules registered for it. Without the configuration none of them is shown — from [juicebar#Requirements[CONFIG]]

## Tests

- A staff member without `entities:role` cannot read the customers from the backend.
- A staff member signed in to organisation A cannot open or change a customer created in organisation B.
- A staff member without `entities:role#admin` choosing the type Organisation gets no rows.
- With `protection` on, a customer another staff member protected is missing from the listing of a staff member who is not an admin of customers.
- Without an `amgshop` configuration no calling-number field and no "Customer group" column appears anywhere in the module.

## Dependencies

### Requires

- WalletLedger as Ledger
- MailHistory as Mails
- PushHistory as Pushes
- PaymentAccounts as Payments
- FormUploads as Forms

## Persona: CustomerEditor

### Summary

A staff member whose role has the customers role.

### Role

- Keeps the organisation's customers — [plays](aim:juicebar.core#Persona:Staff)

### Access

- The customers module — [accesses](aim:juicebar.entities)

## Persona: CustomerAdmin

### Summary

A staff member whose role has `entities:role#admin`: they also see the organisations, the customers other staff protected, and keep the attribute fields.

### Role

- Keeps the organisation's customers, the protected ones and the attribute fields included — [plays](aim:juicebar.core#Persona:Staff)

### Access

- The customers module — [accesses](aim:juicebar.entities)

## Persona: CustomerSuperAdmin

### Summary

A staff member whose role has `entities:role#super-admin` in the organisation they are signed in to: they reach the customers of every organisation.

### Role

- Keeps the customers of every organisation — [plays](aim:juicebar.core#Persona:Staff)

### Access

- The customers module — [accesses](aim:juicebar.entities)

## Record: Customer

### Summary

One customer the project keeps: a person, a company or an organisation.

### Schema

```schema
id: string required unique
type: string ref(juicebar.entities#CustomerType.prop)
salutation: string
sex: string
title: string
firstname: string
lastname: string
name: string
taxNumber: string
email: string
phone: string
mobilephone: string
languages: list(string)
groups: list(juicebar.entities#CustomerGroup)
addresses: list(part(juicebar.entities#CustomerAddress))
attributes: map(string)
wallets: list(part(juicebar.entities#Wallet))
media: list(part(juicebar.entities#CustomerFile))
images: list(part(juicebar.entities#CustomerImage))
form_data: string
organisation_id: string ref(juicebar.core#Organisation.id)
protected: string
noDelete: boolean
created: datetime
updated: datetime
```

### Constraints

- `salutation` is `Mr`, `Mrs` or `Diverse` and `sex` is `Male`, `Female` or `Diverse`, stored in English whatever the admin's language; `name` is the company or organisation name.
- `languages` holds `German`, `English`, `French`, `Croatian`, `Italian` and whatever else staff typed in.
- `attributes` holds, under each attribute field's `property`, the value given for it, of any JSON shape: a text, a number, a date, a switch, or one text per language. It also holds the calling numbers (`phoneCallingNumber`, `mobilephoneCallingNumber`), an organisation's payment account id (`account_id`) and fees (`fee`, `article_fee`), `activated`, and a wallet address of its own (`wallet`).
- `attributes` also holds `files`: the files the customer sent with a form, each with its id, its name and its kind of file. `form_data` is the form entry the customer came in with.
- `protected` is the id of the staff member who protected the customer; `noDelete` is set by the backend for a customer that must stay, never by staff.
- A customer some backends synchronise carries its number there under `mappings`, such as the SAP customer number.

### Immutable

- `organisation_id`

### Bindings

- binds: `projects/juicebar/src/lib/core/modules/entities/entities.types.ts#Entity` — as: model
- provenance: inferred

## Record: CustomerAddress

### Summary

One postal address of a customer.

### Schema

```schema
id: string required
type: string
name: string
street: string
street2: string
postcode: string
city: string
country: string
active: boolean
```

### Constraints

- `type` is `shipping`, `invoice`, `home` or `business`; an address stored without one is `default`. `country` is a country code of the admin's list.

### Bindings

- binds: `projects/juicebar/src/lib/core/modules/entities/entities.types.ts#EntityAddress` — as: model
- provenance: inferred

